\end{align*}
where $\mathbf{Q}_k^{(t)}$ is the quadratic term defined in \cref{sec:notation2} \textcolor{black}{(see the proof of Theorem 2 of \cite{agterberg_estimating_2022} for details on this expansion)}.  
Without loss of generality consider the case $k = 1$.  
Recall we assume $t_0$ is such that \cref{thm:twoinfty} holds.  For $t = t_0 + 1$, where $t_0$ is such that \cref{thm:twoinfty} holds, on the event $\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{main}}^{t,1} \cap \mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{Good}}$, 
