Take any $\mathcal{T}$ such that $\mathcal{T} = \mathcal{C} \times_1 {\mathbf{U}}_1 \times {\mathbf{U}}_2 \times {\mathbf{U}}_3 \in \Theta(\lambda,\kappa,\frac{\mu_0}{2},\sigma,\sigma_{\min})$, and suppose ${\mathbf{U}}_1$ is such that  $\| \big( {\mathbf{U}}_1 \big)_{\cdot, r_k} \|_{\infty} \leq \frac{\mu_0}{2}\sqrt{\frac{1}{p_1}}$. Let $\mathcal{H}_0$ denote the hypothesis space with point mass at $\mathcal{T}$, and let $\pi_{\mathcal{H}_0}$ denote the prior on this set.  We will construct an alternative hypothesis space $\mathcal{H}_1$ with prior given point mass $\pi_{\mathcal{H}_1}$ of the form
